    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d164">

                <pb facs="0213" n="153" xml:id="pg153"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Denby to Mr. Olney</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-10-01"><hi rendition="#italic">October 1, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Nov. 8.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2379.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    telegram received from Messrs. Hixson and Newell; also a copy of my reply
                    thereto; also a copy of my communication to the Tsung-li Yamên relating to the
                    complaints made by the commissioners that the proceedings are impeded, and
                    asking that stringent orders be issued to the viceroy ordering him to facilitate
                    in every way the labors of the commission.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Denby</hi></signed>.</closer>





